# Everything here that is a secret, or is derived from one, stays out of git.
#
#   .author.env    the authoring PF's admin password (up.sh generates it; it becomes the archive's)
#   keys/          the suite clients' PRIVATE JWKs (gen-keys.sh). Test keys are still keys: the
#                  secrets-guard workflow does not grade intent, and neither does anyone who finds one
#                  in a public repo.
#   secrets.env    the generated test-user password and SSF introspection client secret
#   data*.zip      the PF configArchive. A PLAIN ZIP that CONTAINS pf.jwk, the system keys and the
#                  admin password hash - see ../build/pingfederate/.gitignore for how that was learned.
#   overlay/       pf.jwk + pingfederate-system-keys.xml lifted out of that archive
#   suite/*.json   suite configurations rendered from suite/*.template.json WITH the private keys in
.author.env
keys/
secrets.env
data*.zip
overlay/
suite/*.json
!suite/*.template.json

# Derived.
.context/
terraform/.terraform/
terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform/terraform.tfstate*
